{
  "title": "Scrape jobs: make status an enum with guarded transitions",
  "description": "A scrape job's state is spread across status, current_step, current_step_started_at, failed_at_step, error_message, retry_count and recipe_id. status is a set of &str constants (server/src/scraping/mod.rs:89-98) stored as TEXT with no CHECK (sqlite baseline up.sql:214); the enriching -> normalizing rename migration shows the value set already drifts. \
Only retry_job (scraping/runner.rs:982-1003, CAS on status = failed and retry_count) and fail_unfinished (scraping/jobs.rs:620-652) check the current status. mark_failed (jobs.rs:592), mark_completed (jobs.rs:655), update_status_and_step (jobs.rs:491), update_current_step_keeping_start (jobs.rs:536) and resume_interrupted_jobs (runner.rs:279-327) overwrite whatever is there, so correctness rests on there being one runner per job (JOB_SLOTS, runner.rs:366). \
Each site maps steps to statuses by its own rules: the run loop (runner.rs:493-501) calls everything but fetch_html parsing, including load_recipe in normalize and edit jobs; retry (runner.rs:968-974) adds normalizing; photo import uses scraping (photo_import.rs:105); normalize and edit jobs are inserted as pending with a step already running (jobs.rs:234-246, 274-284). \
Representable but wrong: a failed job keeps current_step (status.rs filters it with string-literal terminal checks at 324/345/396); failed with failed_at_step NULL (fail_unfinished); completed with recipe_id NULL. recipe_id has three sources: save_recipe mid-run (steps/save_recipe.rs:378), mark_completed, and the step output for older rows (jobs.rs:469-480, api/scrape/get.rs:90-104). \
Want: a Diesel-mapped Rust enum, a CHECK migration, one step -> status function, and transition functions that UPDATE ... \
WHERE status IN (allowed predecessors) and error on zero rows. \
Add CHECKs tying failed to error_message and completed to recipe_id only after checking prod rows (no data deletion; backfill if needed). \
Server only; the typed API field and client changes are p3-sm-scrape-status-typed-api, timeouts are p3-sm-scrape-job-hung-timeout. make pipeline should produce no data/ diffs. \
Found in the 2026-11-07 implicit-state-machine audit; line numbers are as of e94669d4ca, so re-check each point before fixing.",
